IMPORT prelude

-- Trust Companies Act 2005 (Singapore) -- who needs a trust business licence (s 3, First and Second Schedules, s 15), the fines
-- and the doubling for corporations (ss 3(4), 7(3), 8, 9, 11, 13(6), 20, 21, 26, 27, 59, 66, 67), approval of directors and
-- resident managers (s 13) and disqualified individuals (s 14(1)), control of shareholdings (ss 16, 20, 21), probate and
-- appointment work a licensed trust company may and may not take (ss 22, 23, 26, 56), dealing ahead of trust orders (s 27),
-- annual accounts (s 30) and unclaimed money (s 60).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TCA2005.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 42 of 2024 (in force 20 June 2025) shown; most recent substantive changes to ss 9, 11 and 14 by Act 12 of 2024 (24 January 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 14 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the licensing perimeter and the duties
-- and offences a trust company, its officers and its shareholders meet. Not encoded: winding up (s 12), MAS control and transfers
-- of business (Parts 3A, 3B), books and audit beyond s 30, inspection and investigation powers (Part 7), disclosure and
-- confidentiality (Part 8, Third Schedule), appeals (Part 9), composition (s 69), and everything left to regulations (minimum
-- financial requirements, fees, prescribed exempt persons).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trust Companies Act 2005 -- licensing and conduct`

§§ `3, First and Second Schedules, 15 -- who needs a licence`

-- First Schedule: trust business is "(a) the provision of services with respect to the creation of an express trust; (b) acting as
-- trustee in relation to an express trust; (c) arranging for any person to act as trustee in respect of an express trust; (d) the
-- provision of trust administration services in relation to an express trust."
-- s 3(1): a person "must not carry on any trust business or hold himself, herself or itself out as carrying on any trust business in
-- or from within Singapore unless that person is a licensed trust company". (3): not a person in the Second Schedule -- a bare
-- trustee; a trustee or administrator of a business trust; a trustee-manager of a registered business trust; "a person preparing or
-- advising on a will"; an executor or administrator of an estate.
-- s 15(1): exempt are (a) a licensed bank and (b) a licensed merchant bank, but ONLY for "(i) the provision of services in relation to
-- the creation of an express trust; (ii) the arrangement for any person to act as trustee ...; or (iii) the provision of trust
-- administration services which are procedural and non-discretionary"; (c) capital markets services licensees for fund management or
-- custodial services; (d) prescribed persons; (e) any person the Authority exempts "by written notice".
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `helping to create an express trust`
    `acting as trustee of an express trust`
    `arranging for someone to act as trustee of an express trust`
    `procedural, non-discretionary administration of an express trust`
    `discretionary administration of an express trust`
    `preparing a will`
    `acting as executor of an estate`

DECLARE Provider IS ONE OF
    `a licensed trust company`
    `an unlicensed company`
    `an individual`
    `a licensed bank`
    `a licensed merchant bank`
    `a person exempted by written notice of the Authority`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is trust business` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `preparing a will` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `acting as executor of an estate` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a bank is exempt for the activity` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `helping to create an express trust` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `arranging for someone to act as trustee of an express trust` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `procedural, non-discretionary administration of an express trust` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider, `the activity` IS AN Activity, `is a Second Schedule specified person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying it on breaches section 3(1)` IF
        `the activity is trust business` `the activity`
    AND (NOT `is a Second Schedule specified person`)
    AND CONSIDER `the provider`
        WHEN `a licensed trust company` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a person exempted by written notice of the Authority` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a licensed bank` THEN NOT (`a bank is exempt for the activity` `the activity`)
        WHEN `a licensed merchant bank` THEN NOT (`a bank is exempt for the activity` `the activity`)
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3(4), 7(3), 8, 9, 11, 13, 20, 21, 26, 27, 59, 66, 67 -- maximum fines`

-- s 3(4): "a fine not exceeding $75,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both and, in the case of a
-- continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $7,500 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
-- s 7(3) licence condition: $100,000, further $10,000 a day. s 8 false application: $50,000 or 12 months. s 9(2) failing to notify a
-- change within 14 days: "shall be guilty of an offence" -- no penalty stated since Act 12 of 2024, so s 66: "a fine not exceeding
-- $12,500". s 11(2) ceasing business while a trust is unadministered: $25,000, further $2,500 a day. s 13(6): $50,000. s 20(1):
-- $50,000. s 21(2): $50,000. s 26(2) accepting a prohibited appointment: no penalty stated, so s 66. s 27(2): $50,000 or 3 years.
-- s 59(3): $50,000, further $5,000 a day.
-- s 67(1): where "a corporation or body corporate is convicted", the fine may be "2 times the maximum amount" -- (2) EXCEPT offences
-- under "section 7(3), 11(2), 13(6), 14(6), 21(2), 28(7) or (8), 29(3), 30(4) or (5), 47(6), 48(5)(b) or 49(6)(b)".
-- The doubling is applied here to the whole maximum, the daily further fine included (an inference: s 67(1) speaks of "the maximum
-- amount that the court could ... impose as a fine for that offence").
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `carrying on trust business without a licence`
    `breaching a licence condition`
    `a false statement in a licence application`
    `failing to notify a change of particulars`
    `ceasing business while a trust is unadministered`
    `appointing a director or resident manager without approval`
    `becoming a controller without approval`
    `holding over 20% of another corporation without approval`
    `accepting guardianship of an infant's person`
    `dealing ahead of a trust's orders`
    `mixing trust assets with the company's own`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying on trust business without a licence` THEN 75000
    WHEN `breaching a licence condition` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a false statement in a licence application` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to notify a change of particulars` THEN 12500
    WHEN `ceasing business while a trust is unadministered` THEN 25000
    WHEN `accepting guardianship of an infant's person` THEN 12500
    OTHERWISE 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying on trust business without a licence` THEN 7500
    WHEN `breaching a licence condition` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ceasing business while a trust is unadministered` THEN 2500
    WHEN `mixing trust assets with the company's own` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 67(2) excludes doubling` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breaching a licence condition` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ceasing business while a trust is unadministered` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `appointing a director or resident manager without approval` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `holding over 20% of another corporation without approval` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying on trust business without a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a false statement in a licence application` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dealing ahead of a trust's orders` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offender is a corporation` AND (NOT `section 67(2) excludes doubling` `the offence`)
    THEN 2 TIMES `the undoubled maximum`
    ELSE `the undoubled maximum`
    WHERE
        `the undoubled maximum` MEANS
            `the base maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS `the further daily fine` `the offence` TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `13 -- approval of resident managers and directors`

-- s 13(1): no appointment of "(a) its resident manager; or (b) its director where, upon appointment, the person -- (i) resides or is
-- to reside in Singapore ...; or (ii) is directly responsible for its business in Singapore ... whether he or she resides in Singapore
-- or elsewhere, unless it has obtained the approval of the Authority". (2): once approved, re-appointment "immediately upon the expiry
-- of the earlier term" needs no fresh approval.
-- (4): the Authority must give a hearing before refusing, except where the person "(a) is an undischarged bankrupt" or "(b) has been
-- convicted ... of an offence -- (i) involving fraud or dishonesty ...; and (ii) punishable with imprisonment for a term of 3 months or
-- more". (5): the proposed appointee need not be heard at all.
DECLARE Appointment IS ONE OF
    `a resident manager`
    `a director living in Singapore`
    `a director abroad directly responsible for Singapore business`
    `a director abroad not responsible for Singapore business`

GIVEN `the appointment` IS AN Appointment, `an immediate re-appointment of an approved person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority's approval is needed` IF
        (NOT `an immediate re-appointment of an approved person`)
    AND CONSIDER `the appointment`
        WHEN `a director abroad not responsible for Singapore business` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Individual HAS
    `convicted of a fraud or dishonesty offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that offence carries 3 months' imprisonment or more` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an unsatisfied judgment debt enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a creditors' compromise still in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under a prohibition order in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ran a financial institution wound up or stripped of its licence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may refuse approval without a hearing` IF
        `the person`'s `an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  (`the person`'s `convicted of a fraud or dishonesty offence` AND `the person`'s `that offence carries 3 months' imprisonment or more`)

§§ `14(1) -- disqualified individuals`

-- s 14(1): without "the prior written consent of the Authority", a licensed trust company must not permit an individual "(a) to act as
-- its officer, executive officer or resident manager; and (b) [if] incorporated in Singapore ... to act as its director" if the
-- individual (c) has a fraud or dishonesty conviction (or one specified in the Third Schedule to the Registration of Criminals Act --
-- not modelled); (d) is an undischarged bankrupt; (e) has an enforcement order for a judgment debt returned unsatisfied; (f) has a
-- creditors' compromise "still in operation"; (g) has a prohibition order "that remains in force"; or (h) was a director of, or
-- directly concerned in managing, a regulated financial institution that was wound up by a court or whose licence was revoked.
-- Note: (c) carries no 3-month threshold, unlike s 13(4).
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `officer`
    `executive officer`
    `resident manager`
    `director`

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has a section 14(1) ground` IF
        `the person`'s `convicted of a fraud or dishonesty offence`
    OR  `the person`'s `an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the person`'s `has an unsatisfied judgment debt enforcement order`
    OR  `the person`'s `in a creditors' compromise still in operation`
    OR  `the person`'s `under a prohibition order in force`
    OR  `the person`'s `ran a financial institution wound up or stripped of its licence`

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Individual, `the role` IS A Role, `the company is incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority's consent is needed for the person to act` IF
        `the person has a section 14(1) ground` `the person`
    AND CONSIDER `the role`
        WHEN `director` THEN `the company is incorporated in Singapore` OR `a director is an officer`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 2: "officer" has the meaning in s 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967, which (as deposited in this repository) "includes (a) any
-- director". So a director of a company incorporated OUTSIDE Singapore is still an "officer" under s 14(1)(a), and the Singapore-only
-- limb (b) adds nothing. Read literally, this flag is TRUE. (Reading the Companies Act definition into s 14 is the encoder's step.)
`a director is an officer` MEANS TRUE

§§ `16, 20 -- controllers`

-- s 16(3): a "20% controller" holds, alone or with associates, "20% or more but less than 50%" of the issued shares, or controls voting
-- power of "20% or more but less than 50%"; a "50% controller" holds "50% or more" of either. An "indirect controller" is one on whose
-- directions the directors are "accustomed or under an obligation ... to act", or who can determine policy, but not an approved
-- director or officer, nor someone whose advice is followed "by reason only" of its being given "in the person's professional
-- capacity".
-- s 16(1): becoming any of these of a licensed trust company "incorporated in Singapore" requires prior approval; (2) for one
-- incorporated outside Singapore, the company notifies "as soon as practicable" after the acquisition.
-- The percentages below are the person's holdings together with associates' (s 16(4)(c)); aggregation itself is not modelled.
GIVEN `shares percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 50% controller` IF
    `shares percent` AT LEAST 50 OR `votes percent` AT LEAST 50

GIVEN `shares percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 20% controller` IF
        (`shares percent` AT LEAST 20 AND `shares percent` LESS THAN 50)
    OR  (`votes percent` AT LEAST 20 AND `votes percent` LESS THAN 50)

GIVEN `the directors act on the person's wishes` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is an approved director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `only because of professional advice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an indirect controller` IF
        `the directors act on the person's wishes`
    AND (NOT `the person is an approved director or officer`)
    AND (NOT `only because of professional advice`)

GIVEN `shares percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes percent` IS A NUMBER, `directs the directors` IS A BOOLEAN, `the company is incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prior approval is needed to become a controller` IF
        `the company is incorporated in Singapore`
    AND (    `is a 20% controller` `shares percent` `votes percent`
         OR  `is a 50% controller` `shares percent` `votes percent`
         OR  `is an indirect controller` `directs the directors` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 20(2): a defence if the person proves "(a) the person was not aware" of the contravention and "(b) ... within 14 days of becoming
-- aware" notified the Authority and took the action it directed. (3): even if aware, a defence if the contravention resulted from an
-- increase in an associate's holding or voting power (a family associate, s 16(4)(c)(i)), the person has no agreement with that
-- associate to act together, and notified "within 14 days of the date of the contravention" and took the directed action.
-- (4): otherwise "it is not a defence ... to prove that the person did not intend to or did not knowingly contravene".
GIVEN `was aware of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused by a family associate's increase` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an agreement with that associate` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify the Authority` IS A NUMBER, `took the directed action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a defence to section 16(1)` IF
        `days to notify the Authority` AT MOST 14
    AND `took the directed action`
    AND (    (NOT `was aware of the contravention`)
         OR  (`caused by a family associate's increase` AND (NOT `has an agreement with that associate`)))

§§ `21 -- holdings in other corporations`

-- s 21(1): a licensed trust company must not, without prior approval, "acquire or hold MORE THAN (a) 20% of the total number of issued
-- shares; or (b) 20% of the voting power, in a corporation, unless it acquires or holds such shares or voting power in the course of
-- acting as a trustee". Note "more than 20%", where s 16 says "20% or more".
GIVEN `shares percent` IS A NUMBER, `votes percent` IS A NUMBER, `held as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding breaches section 21(1)` IF
        (`shares percent` GREATER THAN 20 OR `votes percent` GREATER THAN 20)
    AND (NOT `held as trustee`)
    AND (NOT `approved`)

§§ `22, 23, 26, 56 -- appointments a licensed trust company may take`

-- s 22: appointed executor, it may apply for probate. s 23(1), (2), (4): a person entitled to probate or administration may authorise
-- it to apply instead; (3) not "in which a will provides that the licensed trust company must not act as executor or in the trusts
-- thereof"; (5) authorised, it is entitled equally with others but "is not on that account alone to be preferred to the widower, widow
-- or next of kin of any intestate".
-- s 26(1): it "must not be" (a) "a guardian of the person of an infant"; (b) a donee of a lasting power of attorney "in relation to the
-- personal welfare" of the donor; (c) a court deputy with power over "personal welfare".
-- s 56(1): it may be appointed trustee "as if [it] were a private individual"; (2) not where the instrument "forbids the appointment of
-- a company".
-- Property-and-affairs powers under a lasting power or deputyship are not named in s 26(1); that they are therefore allowed is an
-- inference.
DECLARE Engagement IS ONE OF
    `executor named in a will`
    `administrator with the will annexed, on authorisation`
    `administrator of an intestate estate, on authorisation`
    `trustee appointed under a power`
    `guardian of an infant's person`
    `lasting power donee for personal welfare`
    `lasting power donee for property and affairs`
    `court deputy for personal welfare`
    `court deputy for property and affairs`

GIVEN `the engagement` IS AN Engagement, `the will or instrument forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensed trust company may take the engagement` IF
    CONSIDER `the engagement`
    WHEN `guardian of an infant's person` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `lasting power donee for personal welfare` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `court deputy for personal welfare` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `administrator with the will annexed, on authorisation` THEN NOT `the will or instrument forbids it`
    WHEN `trustee appointed under a power` THEN NOT `the will or instrument forbids it`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `27 -- trust orders first`

-- s 27(1): a licensed trust company "or any of its employees involved in the management of the assets of an express trust must not
-- enter into any transaction for the purchase or sale of any capital markets products for its, his or her own account unless all
-- instructions to purchase or sell the capital markets products of the same class for the account of the trust have been fulfilled".
GIVEN `manages express trust assets` IS A BOOLEAN, `own-account trade in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN, `trust instructions of the same class unfulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trade breaches section 27(1)` IF
    `manages express trust assets` AND `own-account trade in capital markets products` AND `trust instructions of the same class unfulfilled`

§§ `30 -- annual accounts`

-- s 30(1)(b): lodge the accounts and auditor's report "within 5 months" after the financial year end; (2) on "a special reason" the
-- Authority "may extend that period by not more than 4 months". (4): late lodgment -- "a fine not exceeding $500 for every day or part
-- of a day that the lodgment is late, subject to a maximum fine of $50,000". s 30(4) is in the s 67(2) list, so no doubling.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `extension months granted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months allowed to lodge accounts` MEANS 5 PLUS `the smaller of` `extension months granted` 4

GIVEN `days late` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum late-lodgment fine` MEANS `the smaller of` (500 TIMES `days late`) 50000

§§ `60 -- unclaimed money`

-- s 60(1): moneys and assets held "as trustee of a trust constituted in Singapore, and unclaimed by the person entitled to them for a
-- period of 6 years after the time when they became payable ... (except where payment has been restrained by order of a court ...)"
-- must be paid into court under s 62 of the Trustees Act 1967; (2) no one's consent is needed.
GIVEN `trust constituted in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `years unclaimed since payable` IS A NUMBER, `payment restrained by court order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the money must be paid into court` IF
        `trust constituted in Singapore`
    AND `years unclaimed since payable` AT LEAST 6
    AND (NOT `payment restrained by court order`)
